import Game.Levels.Compose.L01_AddSelf

World "Composition"
Title "Composition and Algebraic Identities"

Introduction "
# Composition

The Master Theorem is **compositional**: the limit of a TP is read off
inductively over its syntax tree. So algebraic identities on TP terms
correspond to identities on their infinite-width limits.

In this world you'll prove a few small structural identities. They look
trivial because they are — that's the point. The Master Theorem
inherits *every* such identity automatically, which is why the TP
language is such a useful intermediate representation.
"
